    {
      "id": "4eGueUkgla6IgrPQb1Gpt",
      "order": 5,
      "layout": "Image",
      "content": {
        "images": [
          "https://d2w9rnfcy7mm78.cloudfront.net/22169275/original_11c0f617883b3d9b318247abbd4d4048.jpg?1686205619?bc=0"
        ],
        "text": [
          "the image is an illustration by [Studio Airport](https://www.instagram.com/studio.airport/?hl=en) to accompany Robin Wall Kimmerer's essay '[The Serviceberry](https://emergencemagazine.org/essay/the-serviceberry/),' in *Emergence Magazine*"
        ],
        "url": "",
        "comments": [
          {
            "id": "dZ5VEYcvG7-X88NC0CFN2",
            "slotIndex": 0,
            "x": 0.27563986368909515,
            "y": 0.10127710127710128,
            "text": "I love how enigmatic these little openings are—and the collision between something very natural, physical, dimensional (the leaves) and something much more flat and constructed (the 2D cutouts, which remind us that this is a photograph of some leaves, not the actual leaves themselves)"
          }
        ]
      },
